=== Module 28 - Grammar Workbench: from a language's EBNF to a working LL(1) parser ===

--- 1. the grammar as the spec writes it ---
grammar: fixtures/ajoda.ebnf
  24 EBNF rules -> 82 BNF productions | 24 rules + 21 helpers = 45 nonterminals | 37 terminals (3 token classes)
  helpers:
    Program_rep1       { FunctionDecl }
    FunctionDecl_opt1  [ ParamList ]
    ParamList_rep1     { "," Param }
    Block_rep1         { Statement }
    IfStmt_opt1        [ "else" ( Block | IfStmt ) ]
    IfStmt_grp2        ( Block | IfStmt )
    ReturnStmt_opt1    [ Expression ]
    LogicalOr_rep1     { "||" LogicalAnd }
    LogicalAnd_rep1    { "&&" Equality }
    Equality_rep1      { ( "==" | "!=" ) Comparison }
    Equality_grp2      ( "==" | "!=" )
    Comparison_rep1    { ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" ) Term }
    Comparison_grp2    ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" )
    Term_rep1          { ( "+" | "-" ) Factor }
    Term_grp2          ( "+" | "-" )
    Factor_rep1        { ( "*" | "/" | "%" ) Unary }
    Factor_grp2        ( "*" | "/" | "%" )
    Unary_grp1         ( "!" | "-" )
    Call_opt1          [ "(" [ ArgList ] ")" ]
    Call_opt2          [ ArgList ]
    ArgList_rep1       { "," Expression }
  nullable: Program Program_rep1 FunctionDecl_opt1 ParamList_rep1 Block_rep1 IfStmt_opt1 ReturnStmt_opt1 LogicalOr_rep1 LogicalAnd_rep1 Equality_rep1 Comparison_rep1 Term_rep1 Factor_rep1 Call_opt1 Call_opt2 ArgList_rep1
  left recursion: none
  LL(1): NO, 1 conflict
    Statement on IDENT:
      [Statement -> AssignStmt]  via Statement -> AssignStmt -> IDENT
      [Statement -> ExprStmt]  via Statement -> ExprStmt -> Expression -> LogicalOr -> LogicalAnd -> Equality -> Comparison -> Term -> Factor -> Unary -> Call -> Primary -> IDENT

--- 2. one repair: fold assignment into ExprStmt ---
grammar: fixtures/ajoda-fixed.ebnf
  23 EBNF rules -> 82 BNF productions | 23 rules + 22 helpers = 45 nonterminals | 37 terminals (3 token classes)
  helpers:
    Program_rep1       { FunctionDecl }
    FunctionDecl_opt1  [ ParamList ]
    ParamList_rep1     { "," Param }
    Block_rep1         { Statement }
    IfStmt_opt1        [ "else" ( Block | IfStmt ) ]
    IfStmt_grp2        ( Block | IfStmt )
    ReturnStmt_opt1    [ Expression ]
    ExprStmt_opt1      [ "=" Expression ]
    LogicalOr_rep1     { "||" LogicalAnd }
    LogicalAnd_rep1    { "&&" Equality }
    Equality_rep1      { ( "==" | "!=" ) Comparison }
    Equality_grp2      ( "==" | "!=" )
    Comparison_rep1    { ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" ) Term }
    Comparison_grp2    ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" )
    Term_rep1          { ( "+" | "-" ) Factor }
    Term_grp2          ( "+" | "-" )
    Factor_rep1        { ( "*" | "/" | "%" ) Unary }
    Factor_grp2        ( "*" | "/" | "%" )
    Unary_grp1         ( "!" | "-" )
    Call_opt1          [ "(" [ ArgList ] ")" ]
    Call_opt2          [ ArgList ]
    ArgList_rep1       { "," Expression }
  nullable: Program Program_rep1 FunctionDecl_opt1 ParamList_rep1 Block_rep1 IfStmt_opt1 ReturnStmt_opt1 ExprStmt_opt1 LogicalOr_rep1 LogicalAnd_rep1 Equality_rep1 Comparison_rep1 Term_rep1 Factor_rep1 Call_opt1 Call_opt2 ArgList_rep1
  left recursion: none
  LL(1): YES  table 45 x 38, 267 of 1710 cells used

parse fixtures/factorial.tokens (42 tokens from Module 16):
  first 12 steps:
    top of stack          lookahead   action
    Program               "fn"        Program -> Program_rep1
    Program_rep1          "fn"        Program_rep1 -> FunctionDecl Program_rep1
    FunctionDecl          "fn"        FunctionDecl -> "fn" IDENT "(" FunctionDecl_opt1 ")" "->" Type Block
    "fn"                  "fn"        match
    IDENT                 IDENT       match
    "("                   "("         match
    FunctionDecl_opt1     IDENT       FunctionDecl_opt1 -> ParamList
    ParamList             IDENT       ParamList -> Param ParamList_rep1
    Param                 IDENT       Param -> IDENT ":" Type
    IDENT                 IDENT       match
    ":"                   ":"         match
    Type                  "i64"       Type -> "i64"
  ACCEPTED: 176 expansions, 41 matches, stack depth up to 16

parse fixtures/missing-semi.tokens (23 tokens from Module 16):
  REJECTED at 3:5: in Call, expected one of "(" ")" "," "=" ";" "||" "&&" "==" "!=" "<" "<=" ">" ">=" "+" "-" "*" "/" "%" but found "return"

--- 3. a left-recursive grammar ---
grammar: fixtures/arith-leftrec.ebnf
  3 EBNF rules -> 7 BNF productions | 3 rules + 0 helpers = 3 nonterminals | 6 terminals (1 token class)
  nullable: (none)
  left recursion: YES
  removed with Paull's algorithm (Module 23):
    Expr -> Term Expr'
    Expr' -> "+" Term Expr' | "-" Term Expr' | epsilon
    Term -> Atom Term'
    Term' -> "*" Atom Term' | epsilon
    Atom -> "(" Expr ")" | INT_LIT
  LL(1): YES  table 5 x 7, 15 of 35 cells used

summary: EBNF read as written | brackets desugared to named helpers | conflicts traced to the rules that cause them | left recursion removed | the finished table parses Module 16's tokens
